    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_7adee295",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: 911_what_is_your_emergency; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The meme depicts a man calling 911 while another man lies on the ground, with text implying the caller is reporting a non-emergency situation involving political discourse. The overall intent is to satirize or mock individuals who engage in politically charged debates, particularly those who claim to defend a political figure without mentioning specific opponents. While not explicitly targeting a protected group with hate speech, the meme uses a dramatic, emergency-response visual to exaggerate the perceived seriousness of political disagreements, which can be seen as harmful by framing political discourse as an emergency. The intent is to provoke laughter or commentary through absurd juxtaposition, but the potential for harm lies in its ability to trivialize genuine emergencies or to stigmatize political debate as inherently dangerous or absurd.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_477efa7a"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
